{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_142219_f7cddf", "exit_code": 0, "text": "## Sales Battlecard: Aurora 14 vs Vantage Pro 16\n\n**Positioning**\nAurora 14 is the portable workstation for owners who need AI compute, memory headroom, and portability. Vantage Pro 16 is the desktop-replacement for buyers who want a bigger screen, more GPU memory, and a longer battery.\n\n**Aurora 14 Strengths**\n1. **Memory & Upgradeability:** 128 GB maximum (vs. 64 GB soldered). Users can start at 32 GB and upgrade. Analysts expect memory to matter more for large AI models.\n2. **Local AI:** 60 TOPS NPU (vs. 40 TOPS) with sufficient memory headroom to run ~30B-parameter open models locally.\n3. **Portability:** 1.65 kg vs. 2.30 kg. Easier to carry to meetings or other locations.\n\n**Vantage Pro 16 Genuine Strengths**\n1. **Screen:** 16-inch IPS, 165 Hz. Reviewers praise it for visualization work.\n2. **GPU Memory:** 24 GB (vs. 16 GB). Advantage for large 3D scenes and bigger GPU-bound models.\n\n**Likely Objections (3 each) & Responses**\n\n*   **Online:** \"The Vantage is $300 cheaper.\"\n    *   **Response:** \"That's a real benefit. However, the Aurora includes a 3-year on-site warranty versus the 1-year depot service that comes with the Vantage\u2014that's 30 months more supported. You save $300 up front but get significantly more peace of mind and service coverage over time.\"\n\n*   **Online:** \"I need more screen real estate.\"\n    *   **Response:** \"We do acknowledge the Vantage has a larger 16-inch display. If you are a professional visualization user who prioritizes screen size above everything else, we'd recommend the Vantage. However, for most owners, the Aurora's OLED panel offers superior contrast and color accuracy.\"\n\n*   **Online:** \"I'm on a tight budget.\"\n    *   **Response:** \"We understand price is a factor. The Vantage is $300 less at launch, but remember that the Aurora comes with 3 years of on-site service vs. 1 year depot service on the Vantage. Depending on your eligibility for volume discounts or rebates, that service difference may offset the upfront cost.\"\n\n**Discovery Question for the Salesperson to Ask**\n1. \"What portion of your workflow is mobile versus stationary? Are you spending more time moving between rooms or at a desk?\"\n\n*If they say \"Mobile\": Push Aurora (lighter weight, more ports, memory upgrades).*\n*If they say \"Stationary\": Push Vantage (bigger screen, more GPU memory, more battery).*", "tokens": {"input": 4609, "output": 624, "total": 5233, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 6764, "timestamp": 1790803346575}